"Vulnerable Customers (LACE Framework)":{
title:"Vulnerable Customers - LACE Framework",
source:"Slide 64",
content:`
<p>This serves as a guide on how to handle vulnerable customers (e.g., mental health concerns, health issues, or inability to pay). If the customer is not eligible for a Promise to Pay arrangement, follow this process:</p>

<h3>L – Listen</h3>
<p>Listen carefully to the customer's concern without interruption. Allow them to fully explain their situation.</p>

<h3>A – Acknowledge</h3>
<p>Acknowledge the customer's concern with empathy and understanding. Show that their situation is heard and respected.</p>

<h3>C – Check</h3>
<p>Clarify and confirm important details if anything is unclear. Ensure you fully understand the customer's situation and needs.</p>

<h3>E – Enable</h3>
<p>Provide clear guidance, educate the customer on available options, and escalate to the appropriate support team when needed.</p>

<div class="warning-box">
<ul>
<li>Do not argue with the customer and do not act as a therapist.</li>
<li>Maintain professionalism at all times while focusing on resolution and support.</li>
</ul>
</div>
`
},

